WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.640
- So my friend Mark Rober has graduated

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.970
from detonating glitter
bombs on package thieves,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.610
to actually catching scammers in the act.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:07.602
And many of you will ask,

00:00:07.602 --> 00:00:11.329
can Mark's evidence
actually be used in court?

00:00:11.329 --> 00:00:12.470
And the answer is,

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.880
it depends, because it always depends,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.670
but probably more likely than not.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.980
There are a couple of
overlapping issues here.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.740
Number one is chain of custody.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.350
When you have evidence, you have to show

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.090
that it is what it purports
to be, and it's authentic.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.885
And Mark can probably
demonstrate this through

00:00:25.885 --> 00:00:28.240
lots and lots of videographic evidence.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.210
- You can call my probation officer,

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.080
I don't know what's happened.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.270
- And then there's the evidentiary issue.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:32.990
A lot of these videos
are going to be hearsay.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.940
It's technically considered
hearsay evidence.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.730
But as you know, if
you watch this channel,

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.200
there are lots of exceptions
and they probably apply here.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.990
And then finally there
are statutory things,

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.281
like rules against videotaping people,

00:00:42.281 --> 00:00:45.860
privacy laws, and here
it gets a little dicey,

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.201
but query whether you have
an expectation of privacy

00:00:47.201 --> 00:00:50.448
if you're engaged in
manifest illegal activity.

00:00:50.448 --> 00:00:52.170
But this is going to change,

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.330
it's going to be case by case.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:54.710
Good for Mark for taking the initiative

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.240
and trying to catch
some of these bad guys.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.210
It's fascinating.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.050
Go watch his video,

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.553
or I'll see you in court.

